The sum of the roots of the first equation is $-m,$ so $2a+2b=-m.$  Then $p-m=0,$ so $p=m.$

Also, from the product of the roots of the first equation, we have $4ab=n.$  From the product of the roots of the second equation, we have $ab=m.$

Therefore, $$\frac{n}p = \frac{4ab}m = 4\cdot\frac{ab}m = 4,$$ so the value of $n/p$ is $\boxed{4}.$ [asy]
